Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-28-2001||05:33 PM||||Let me explain the situation. There is the plastic cylinderical part that fits into the actual clutch pedal (really small, maybe 1/4 across) and then there is the little snap that makes surei t doesn't come out. Well, mine broke off, so I have to reach down there to push it in. Heres my idea. just drill a little hole into the 1/4 cylindrical part that goes into the pedal, and put a washer and small screw in there. Anyone ever tried this? Sure would be a *****  for the next owner to figure out though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||LivoniaFieroGT||04-28-2001||09:57 PM||||Sounds like it would work.... looked at mine and looks feasible.   I however, just used a jumper wire into the connector and bypassed the neutral start.  I always put clutch in so it never matters.  Beware to the thief who jumps in though.<P>||||reg||1
